{"text": "MILWAUKEE Office of Academics\n\n5225 W. Vliet Street\nPUBLIC SCHOOLS Milwaukee, W! 53208\n\n(414) 777-7806 \u00ab mps.milwaukee.k12.Wi.us\nDecember 21, 2018\n\nDear Paxtyn Merten,\n\nThis communication is a written response regarding information request 18190774, Thank you for\nyour interest in the Milwaukee Public Schools (MPS) Human Growth and Development (HGD)\nCurriculum,\n\nMPS has made our HGD curriculum available online for the ease of sharing it with our parents\nand any other schools that may have an interest in using it. We have lessons at every grade level\nstarting at 5-year old kindergarten (K5) through ninth grade, The identified curriculum can be\nfound on the Health Education page of the MPS portal as well as translated into eight other\nlanguages. Due to the size of the documents, copies of the direct links to the curriculum by grade\nlevel are listed below:\n\nulum Kindergarten - English\nulum Grade 1 - English\nium Grade 2 -\nium Grade 3 -\nulum Grade 4 - English\n\nHuman Growth Development Curr\nHuman Growth Development Cui\nHuman Growth Development Cui\nHuman Growth Development C\nHuman Growth Development Curr\nHuman Growth Development Curriculum Grade 5 - English\nHuman Growth Development Curriculum Grade 6 -\nHuman Growth Development Curriculum Grade 7 - English\nHuman Growth Development Curriculum Grade 8 - Eng!\nHuman Growth Development Curriculum High School - English\n\nIf you have additional questions about the curriculum, please feel free to contact Brett Fuller,\nhealth and physical education curriculum specialist at fullertba@milwaukee.k12,wi.us or\n414-475-8057.\n\nNeremiah Holiday, Ph.D.\nInterim Chief Academic Officer\n\nCe: Keith Posley, Ed.D., Superintendent of Schools\nSue Saller, Manager, Superintendent Initiatives\nMaricha Harris, Special Assistant to the Superintendent\nJacqueline Mann, Director, Office of Board Governance\n\nStart. Stay. Succeed.\nComiensa. Qu\u00e9date, Trinnfit.",
